IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc11-general`

-- general: tests of ccc11-general.l4 (Part VIII.1, sections 320.36 to 320.4: use of samples and results, refusal to take a sample, approvals, designations; section 320.38 is machinery)
-- Expected values are written by hand from the text of the provision, beside each assertion, before the run; none is copied from the code's output.
-- JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE / NOTHING: the text says yes / the text says no in its own words / not covered.

-- A stand-in for the INPUT "the general penalty of section 787(1)" (Part XXVII, another part): arbitrary figures, chosen only to show the input is returned unchanged.
`s 787(1) test: a stand-in general penalty` MEANS Punishment WITH
    `mode` IS `on summary conviction`
    `maximum imprisonment` IS `imprisonment for a term of` `ninety days`
    `minimum imprisonment` IS `no imprisonment is stated`
    `maximum fine` IS `a fine of` 777
    `minimum fine` IS `no fine is stated`

GIVEN p IS A Punishment
GIVETH A `Mode of proceeding`
`s 320.36 test: the mode of the limb` MEANS p's `mode`

§ `s 320.36: use of bodily substances and of results`
-- arguments for (1): the substance was obtained under this Part ; the use is for a purpose other than an analysis under this Part
#ASSERT `s 320.36(1) the use of the bodily substance is prohibited` TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- the prohibition applies
#ASSERT `s 320.36(1) the use of the bodily substance is prohibited` FALSE TRUE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- not obtained under this Part
#ASSERT `s 320.36(1) the use of the bodily substance is prohibited` TRUE FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- used for an analysis under this Part
-- The prohibition as a regulative rule (SHANT): a trace in which the person does the forbidden act is printed (a breach); the stable binary cannot assert it (NOTES.md).
#TRACE `s 320.36(1) no person shall use a bodily substance obtained under this Part for another purpose` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 320.36 any person` DOES `s 320.36(1) use a bodily substance obtained under this Part for a purpose other than an analysis under this Part` AT 1
#TRACE `s 320.36(2) no person shall use or disclose the results for another purpose` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 320.36 any person` DOES `s 320.36(2) use, disclose or allow the disclosure of the results obtained under this Part of an evaluation, physical coordination test or analysis of a bodily substance` AT 1
-- arguments for (3): the results are of an evaluation, test or analysis referred to in (2) ; the disclosure is to the person to whom they relate ; the results are made anonymous ; for statistical or research purposes
#ASSERT `s 320.36(3) the results may be disclosed` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- disclosed to the person to whom they relate
#ASSERT `s 320.36(3) the results may be disclosed` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- to any other person if anonymous and for statistical or research purposes
#ASSERT `s 320.36(3) the results may be disclosed` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- anonymous but not for statistical or research purposes: not covered
#ASSERT `s 320.36(3) the results may be disclosed` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- for research but not anonymous: not covered
#ASSERT `s 320.36(3) the results may be disclosed` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not results referred to in (2)
-- arguments for (2): the results were obtained under this Part ; the person uses, discloses or allows disclosure ; it is for the purpose of administering or enforcing a federal or provincial Act related to drugs, alcohol or operating ; permitted by (3) (by s 320.36(3))
#ASSERT `s 320.36(2) the use or disclosure of the results is prohibited` TRUE TRUE FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- the prohibition applies
#ASSERT `s 320.36(2) the use or disclosure of the results is prohibited` TRUE TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- "except for the purpose of the administration or enforcement of a federal or provincial Act"
#ASSERT `s 320.36(2) the use or disclosure of the results is prohibited` TRUE TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- permitted by subsection (3)
#ASSERT `s 320.36(2) the use or disclosure of the results is prohibited` TRUE TRUE FALSE NOTHING EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- subsection (3) is not made out (it answers NOTHING when its gate is unmet): no exception, so the prohibition stands (fork F26)
#ASSERT `s 320.36(2) the use or disclosure of the results is prohibited` TRUE TRUE FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- subsection (3) says no: the prohibition stands
#ASSERT `s 320.36(2) the use or disclosure of the results is prohibited` FALSE TRUE FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- the results were not obtained under this Part
#ASSERT `s 320.36(2) the use or disclosure of the results is prohibited` TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- no use or disclosure
#ASSERT `s 320.36(4) everyone commits an offence who contravenes subsection 320.36(1) or (2)` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- contravenes subsection (1)
#ASSERT `s 320.36(4) everyone commits an offence who contravenes subsection 320.36(1) or (2)` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- contravenes subsection (2)
#ASSERT `s 320.36(4) everyone commits an offence who contravenes subsection 320.36(1) or (2)` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- contravenes neither
#ASSERT `s 320.36(4) everyone commits an offence who contravenes subsection 320.36(1) or (2)` NOTHING (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- not covered
#ASSERT `s 320.36(4) everyone commits an offence who contravenes subsection 320.36(1) or (2)` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- contravenes (2), whatever (1) says
#ASSERT `s 320.36 test: the mode of the limb` (`s 320.36(4) the punishment for an offence under subsection 320.36(4)` `s 787(1) test: a stand-in general penalty`) EQUALS `on summary conviction`   -- the penalty is the input s 787(1) penalty: returned unchanged
#ASSERT `s 320.36(4) the class of the offence`  EQUALS `an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- "commits an offence punishable on summary conviction"

§ `s 320.37: refusal to take a sample; no liability`
-- arguments for (1): practitioner (by s 320.11) ; technician (blood) (by s 320.11) ; the only ground is their refusal to take a sample for the purposes of this Part ; they have a reasonable excuse
#ASSERT `s 320.37(1) the qualified medical practitioner or qualified technician shall not be found guilty of an offence by reason only of their refusal to take a sample of blood` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- a practitioner who refused with a reasonable excuse
#ASSERT `s 320.37(1) the qualified medical practitioner or qualified technician shall not be found guilty of an offence by reason only of their refusal to take a sample of blood` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- a technician who refused with a reasonable excuse
#ASSERT `s 320.37(1) the qualified medical practitioner or qualified technician shall not be found guilty of an offence by reason only of their refusal to take a sample of blood` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- no reasonable excuse: this subsection gives no immunity
#ASSERT `s 320.37(1) the qualified medical practitioner or qualified technician shall not be found guilty of an offence by reason only of their refusal to take a sample of blood` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) FALSE TRUE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- the charge rests on more than the refusal
#ASSERT `s 320.37(1) the qualified medical practitioner or qualified technician shall not be found guilty of an offence by reason only of their refusal to take a sample of blood` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- neither a practitioner nor a technician
#ASSERT `s 320.37(1) the qualified medical practitioner or qualified technician shall not be found guilty of an offence by reason only of their refusal to take a sample of blood` NOTHING (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- practitioner status not covered
-- arguments for (2): practitioner ; technician ; takes a sample under this Part ; what was done was necessary ; done with reasonable care and skill
#ASSERT `s 320.37(2) the qualified medical practitioner or qualified technician incurs liability for doing what was necessary to take the sample` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- no liability: a practitioner
#ASSERT `s 320.37(2) the qualified medical practitioner or qualified technician incurs liability for doing what was necessary to take the sample` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- no liability: a technician
#ASSERT `s 320.37(2) the qualified medical practitioner or qualified technician incurs liability for doing what was necessary to take the sample` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not with reasonable care and skill: the immunity does not reach it
#ASSERT `s 320.37(2) the qualified medical practitioner or qualified technician incurs liability for doing what was necessary to take the sample` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not necessary to take the sample
#ASSERT `s 320.37(2) the qualified medical practitioner or qualified technician incurs liability for doing what was necessary to take the sample` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not a sample taken under this Part
#ASSERT `s 320.37(2) the qualified medical practitioner or qualified technician incurs liability for doing what was necessary to take the sample` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- neither a practitioner nor a technician: not covered

§ `s 320.39: approvals by the Attorney General of Canada (powers)`
-- arguments: acts by order ; the thing is of the kind the paragraph names
#ASSERT `s 320.39(a) the Attorney General of Canada may, by order, approve the device` TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- a device designed to ascertain alcohol in a person's blood
#ASSERT `s 320.39(a) the Attorney General of Canada may, by order, approve the device` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not such a device
#ASSERT `s 320.39(a) the Attorney General of Canada may, by order, approve the device` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not by order
#ASSERT `s 320.39(b) the Attorney General of Canada may, by order, approve the equipment` TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- equipment designed to ascertain a drug in a person's body
#ASSERT `s 320.39(b) the Attorney General of Canada may, by order, approve the equipment` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not such equipment
#ASSERT `s 320.39(c) the Attorney General of Canada may, by order, approve the instrument` TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- an instrument designed to analyse a breath sample
#ASSERT `s 320.39(c) the Attorney General of Canada may, by order, approve the instrument` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not such an instrument
#ASSERT `s 320.39(d) the Attorney General of Canada may, by order, approve the container` TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- a container designed to receive a blood sample
#ASSERT `s 320.39(d) the Attorney General of Canada may, by order, approve the container` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not such a container

§ `s 320.4: designations by the Attorney General (powers)`
-- arguments for (a): made by the Attorney General ; of a person ; as qualified to operate an approved instrument
#ASSERT `s 320.4(a) the Attorney General may designate the person as qualified to operate an approved instrument` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- a person, to operate an approved instrument
#ASSERT `s 320.4(a) the Attorney General may designate the person as qualified to operate an approved instrument` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- a class of persons: paragraph (a) names only "a person"
#ASSERT `s 320.4(a) the Attorney General may designate the person as qualified to operate an approved instrument` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not made by the Attorney General
#ASSERT `s 320.4(a) the Attorney General may designate the person as qualified to operate an approved instrument` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- for another purpose
-- arguments for (b)(i), (b)(ii), (c): made by the Attorney General ; of a person or class of persons ; for the purpose
#ASSERT `s 320.4(b)(i) the Attorney General may designate the person or class of persons as qualified to take samples of blood` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- a person or class, to take samples of blood
#ASSERT `s 320.4(b)(i) the Attorney General may designate the person or class of persons as qualified to take samples of blood` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- for another purpose
#ASSERT `s 320.4(b)(ii) the Attorney General may designate the person or class of persons as qualified to analyze samples of bodily substances` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- a person or class, to analyse samples of bodily substances
#ASSERT `s 320.4(b)(ii) the Attorney General may designate the person or class of persons as qualified to analyze samples of bodily substances` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not made by the Attorney General
#ASSERT `s 320.4(c) the Attorney General may designate the person or class of persons as qualified to certify that an alcohol standard is suitable for use with an approved instrument` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- a person or class, to certify an alcohol standard
#ASSERT `s 320.4(c) the Attorney General may designate the person or class of persons as qualified to certify that an alcohol standard is suitable for use with an approved instrument` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not of a person or class

